      "side": 1,
      "message": "Happy to drop it — nothing on our side depends on it. The consumers only look up the Configuration.\u003cType\u003e records under the platform object; the Inventory.Item.Platform interface itself is unused (FOUND() matches against the in-memory passedProbes list rather than D-Bus, and AddObject is initialized separately).\n\nOne question on scope: this comes from entity-manager creating Inventory.Item.\u003cType\u003e for every config unconditionally, and the Type enum already has values with no PDI interface behind them — NVMe is used by four in-tree configs and produces xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.NVMe today. Is that the same problem (just grandfathered)? It decides whether this belongs in this series or is a general entity-manager cleanup.\n\nThe catch is that dropping it needs a Type \u003d\u003d \"Platform\" special case in postBoardToDBus() — the schema can\u0027t influence this, since entity-manager only reads the Type string.",
